madvise and getrandom without the Linux option: BSD systems have both,
and programs and crates written for Linux call them. madvise's advice
constants (MADV_NORMAL to MADV_DONTNEED, and MADV_FREE) and its
declaration leave the Linux option's block, the function is built with
posix_madvise, and <abi-bits/random.h> no longer refuses to be included
without the Linux option. The Radix system layer builds the Linux
option's getrandom (options/linux/generic/sys-random.cpp) and installs
its <sys/random.h> and <sys/sysmacros.h> (ports/mlibc/build.sh), which
need nothing of Linux's.

